{
  "version": 1,
  "notes": [
    "One sheet = one Codex image call. Cells are named left to right, top to bottom.",
    "grid is [columns, rows]. Dense grids on purpose: many small cells per image saves Codex usage (the user prefers more, smaller images).",
    "A sheet lists its cells directly (with cellDefaults) or as 'groups' in grid order; each group has its own kind, size, out folder and optional atlas.",
    "kind: tile (seamless texture), sprite (background removed), frame (background removed, kept square for 9-slice), concept (model reference, not shipped), icon (square, full cell), additive (glow on black).",
    "size: target size in pixels of each cell after slicing (longest side).",
    "out: 'ui' = client/src/assets/ui (bundled by Vite), 'concept' = art/source only, others go to client/public/assets/<out>/.",
    "atlas: cells with the same atlas name are packed into one image + JSON with UV rects instead of single files."
  ],
